{"id": "EUVD-2026-59712", "enisaUuid": "a51425d9-52db-3845-aadf-b8f2f4d93639", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\npinctrl: devicetree: don't free uninitialized dev_name on error path\n\ndt_remember_or_free_map() duplicates dev_name for each map entry. If\nkstrdup_const() fails, dt_free_map() frees dev_name in all num_maps\nentries, including entries that have not been initialized.\n\nSome pinctrl drivers, including pinctrl-imx, allocate the map with\nkmalloc() and leave dev_name for the core to initialize. The untouched\nentries therefore contain uninitialized data which is passed to\nkfree_const().\n\nReproduced on qemu's mcimx6ul-evk (pinctrl-imx) with failslab injection\nwhile binding the pinctrl-consuming device, under KASAN:\n\n  BUG: KASAN: double-free in dt_free_map+0x34/0xa4\n  Free of addr c425a900 by task init/1\n   kfree from dt_free_map+0x34/0xa4\n   dt_free_map from dt_remember_or_free_map+0x184/0x198\n   dt_remember_or_free_map from pinctrl_dt_to_map+0x33c/0x4c8\n   pinctrl_dt_to_map from create_pinctrl+0x9c/0x5c0\n\nInitialize all dev_name fields to NULL before duplicating the device\nname, making the full-map cleanup safe after a partial failure.", "datePublished": "2026-08-15T12:27:38", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-16T19:05:52", "baseScore": 7.8, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:L/AC:L/PR:L/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H", "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/e3cfb22bad363bebcfd55d909e12d499cb8c5490", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/1586423da2739a80871ef6240016fcb9c7339bfb", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/dec5f0a8080502908dec5e35597c7ae07d533a3b", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/929f6396baade89999ec8a1281232c101cbc727d", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/321fe3584a8298386938130d138191aa35040b75", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/ad0ad3c228b6f76fde10f32047e0ec5fbc109dc8", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/9d00a5ac7cd3d32ae61140f4b8a62f136de84e7d", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/015b5bcbcb622b32317642be91a7f79aa5413649"], "aliases": ["GHSA-63f7-w376-3432", "CVE-2026-74519"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.15, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "03140d21-98c2-3522-b95e-1bba0c3b43c5", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "be4c60b563edee3712d392aaeb0943a768df7023 <dec5f0a8080502908dec5e35597c7ae07d533a3b"}, {"id": "0d406f40-65fc-3059-884f-76632c939b4a", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "be4c60b563edee3712d392aaeb0943a768df7023 <ad0ad3c228b6f76fde10f32047e0ec5fbc109dc8"}, {"id": "13d2e03a-5e4b-3c8f-8c44-0af59b47f717", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "4.9.244 <4.10"}, {"id": "2e3b10b7-5ed3-351a-8a78-90180ff04bb6", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "4.4.244 <4.5"}, {"id": "35214b5b-4fc5-38b6-8281-2ba3747c7a89", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "679c4f27b8958b65bb51d1c3dfdbf3befe4a33a3"}, {"id": "3be231c8-e616-3b01-82bb-ff4a2f256700", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "03f69244302d7954f42f528ea2d45903ebbf59f3"}, {"id": "4ff7f91a-e1f2-3877-8a6c-c44f7dde1af9", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.151"}, {"id": "6a135a49-df86-3140-bb87-ebf549da8d8f", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "be4c60b563edee3712d392aaeb0943a768df7023 <015b5bcbcb622b32317642be91a7f79aa5413649"}, {"id": "71e2cf88-927c-3164-8b06-4ff47b9abe2e", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "5.4.7 <5.5"}, {"id": "7253d8c8-acdc-3d0c-9489-e571eeeeb4fc", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.103"}, {"id": "79956a1c-671c-3113-86bc-55bdd38e9a42", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 5.15.216"}, {"id": "